cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use claude-mac-patrol in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "claude-mac-patrol"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/claude-mac-patrol"
url: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/claude-mac-patrol"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free janitor for machines running agent CLIs such as Claude Code, plus the
  field procedure it came from. Closes orphaned MCP children and stale agent sessions,
  restarts stuck daemons it owns, and reports what it must not touch. Every verdict comes
  from a delta of two CPU-time snapshots, never from the lifetime average that ps %CPU
  reports. Standard library only, no telemetry, no network. Free, MIT.
keywords:
  - macos
  - process-management
  - agent-operations
  - claude-code
  - observability
